[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every wrong-date report as one parser bug. The reports hold
two problems. Each now has its own ticket.

## What is in #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table groups by the tenant's locale and booking form, not by intake's browser guess.

## The problems

1. **Parser reads dates month-first** ([ticket](https://github.com/techybolek/mega/issues/1)).
   Every tenant writes day-first, so months and days flip. This is the one the queued fix covers. The table's note flags a few reports that read as a
   one-day move, likely time zones; the desk files them here, and that is a guess until engineering checks.
2. **booking-v3 form hint says `MM/DD/YYYY`** ([ticket](https://github.com/techybolek/mega/issues/2)).
   People at day-first tenants type what the hint tells them. The parser fix does not reach this.

<Callout>
Not one issue, not one fix. Only problem 1 is covered by the queued fix.
</Callout>

## Why the merge went wrong

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone, and the subjects
match across both problems. A new decision record should replace it.

